# BarkerLink Verible lint waivers (project house style) - see DECISIONS D-0108.
# RTL is portable Verilog-2001 (iverilog/verilator/yosys), not Google-SV style.
# These three default rules conflict with that house style and are disabled
# project-wide; all other Verible rules remain enforced (zero-warning gate).
#
# UPPER_SNAKE_CASE constants/state names are the universal Verilog convention.
-parameter-name-style
# Untyped localparam/parameter (with explicit width) is standard Verilog-2001.
-explicit-parameter-storage-type
# `always @*` is valid Verilog-2001 combinational style (we keep .v, not .sv).
-always-comb
